# Minimal reverse proxy: Caddy handles HTTPS automatically (obtains and
# renews a Let's Encrypt certificate for the domain below) and forwards
# every request to the "nginx" service over the internal Docker network --
# nginx itself is never exposed to the internet directly (see
# docker-compose.prod.yml).
#
# Replace ton-domaine.com with your real domain before deploying. It must
# already have a DNS A (and/or AAAA) record pointing at this server's public
# IP, and ports 80/443 must be reachable from the internet -- Caddy uses
# port 80 for the ACME HTTP-01 challenge (and to redirect plain HTTP to
# HTTPS) and port 443 to serve the certificate it obtains.

ton-domaine.com {
	reverse_proxy nginx:80
}
